IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sumlma-member`

-- Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999 (Cth) -- the amounts computed from the formulas recovered on
-- 2026-10-24, beside sumlma-member.l4 (unchanged, where more than one death beneficiary still answers `not covered`).
--
-- The sidecar ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00518.formulas.md gives the formulas the text deposit lost:
--   * s 17(1A): All unclaimed money as at the end of the unclaimed money day - Former unclaimed money;
--   * ss 17(2AA), 20QF(4), 21E(4), 22B(4), 24G(3): Amount payable under subsection (2) x (Death benefit for the death
--     beneficiary / Total death benefits) -- the same formula for unclaimed money, inactive low-balance accounts, eligible rollover
--     fund accounts, voluntary payments and lost member accounts;
--   * s 20H(4) (former temporary residents): Total of the excess and any interest that would be payable under subsection (2A) apart
--     from subsection (3) x (Total described in paragraph (3)(a) for the death beneficiary / Sum of the totals described in
--     paragraph (3)(a) for all the death beneficiaries), used only where that total falls short of the sum (s 20H(3)(b)).
-- The death benefits each beneficiary would have been paid are what the Commissioner is satisfied of: inputs.
--
-- SEAT: the member, or a death beneficiary of a member who has died, as in sumlma-member.l4. Edition: the compilation
-- sumlma-member.l4 encodes, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00518.txt. BASELINE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act -- amounts, computed`

§§ `s 17(1A) -- how much my fund pays the Commissioner`

-- s 17(1A) "where: former unclaimed money means any of the unclaimed money that, between the unclaimed money day and the day on
-- which the superannuation provider gives the statement ... (a) the superannuation provider pays to a person who is entitled to it;
-- or (b) otherwise ceases to be unclaimed money".
@export How much of the unclaimed money must my fund pay the Commissioner for an unclaimed money day (s 17(1A))?
GIVEN `all unclaimed money at the end of the day` IS A NUMBER @desc All the unclaimed money the fund held at the end of the unclaimed money day, in dollars
      `former unclaimed money` IS A NUMBER @desc Unclaimed money the fund paid to the person entitled, or that otherwise stopped being unclaimed, before it gave its statement, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much unclaimed money must my fund pay` MEANS
    max 0 (`all unclaimed money at the end of the day` MINUS `former unclaimed money`)

§§ `ss 17(2AA), 20QF(4), 21E(4), 22B(4), 24G(3) -- my share as a death beneficiary`

-- "the Commissioner must pay the [amount] under subsection (2) by paying to each death beneficiary the amount worked out using the
-- following formula:" Amount payable x (Death benefit for the death beneficiary / Total death benefits). With one beneficiary the
-- fraction is 1, as the notes say. NOTHING if no death benefit is stated (the formula would divide by nil).
@export A member has died and the ATO holds their super for the death beneficiaries. How much is my share, from the death benefit I would have been paid (ss 17(2AA), 20QF(4), 21E(4), 22B(4), 24G(3))?
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the Commissioner holds for the member who died, in dollars
      `my death benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc The death benefit the fund would have had to pay you, as the Commissioner is satisfied, in dollars
      `total death benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the death benefits the fund would have had to pay all the death beneficiaries, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my share from my death benefit` MEANS
    IF `total death benefits` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the amount` TIMES (`my death benefit` DIVIDED BY `total death benefits`))

§§ `s 20H(3), (4) -- my share as a death beneficiary of a former temporary resident`

-- s 20H(3): each death beneficiary is paid "(a) the total of the amounts the Commissioner is satisfied the superannuation providers
-- would have been required to pay the death beneficiary; or (b) if the total of the excess and any interest that would be payable
-- under subsection (2AA) or (2A) apart from this subsection is less than the sum of the totals described in paragraph (a) for all
-- the death beneficiaries -- the amount worked out for the death beneficiary using the formula in subsection (4)".
@export A former temporary resident has died. How much must the Commissioner pay me as a death beneficiary (s 20H(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the excess and interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The excess held for the person who died, with the interest that would be payable on it, in dollars
      `my total` IS A NUMBER @desc The total the funds would have had to pay you because of the death, in dollars
      `the sum of all the beneficiaries' totals` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of those totals for all the death beneficiaries, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much is my share as a death beneficiary of a former temporary resident` MEANS
    IF `the sum of all the beneficiaries' totals` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the excess and interest` LESS THAN `the sum of all the beneficiaries' totals`
         THEN JUST (`the excess and interest` TIMES (`my total` DIVIDED BY `the sum of all the beneficiaries' totals`))
         ELSE JUST `my total`
